+/// The size of a pooled block, at most the device's `maxMemoryAllocationSize`. raphael: 24 MB, not 64. The GPU's memory
+/// is one fixed pool of 1268 MB for every process, and a pool's next block is as large as all its blocks so far: with
+/// 64 MB backboardd took the pool in steps of 68 MB (eight of them in 5 s at the first app, 760 MB held at 8 min). A
+/// request past half a block (12 MB) still gets a block of its own size; two full-screen targets of 11.5 MB share one.
+pub(super) const BLOCK_BYTES: u64 = 24 << 20;
 
